These terms apply when you use LearnInsurance, run by [TO FILL: operator name]. By using the site you agree to them.

## Educational only, not advice

LearnInsurance explains insurance words in general terms so they are easier to understand.

- It is **not insurance, legal, tax or financial advice**, and it doesn't recommend any product, company or decision.
- What is covered under a real policy depends on **that policy's own wording**, the insurer, and the laws of your state. Always check your policy, or ask a licensed agent, broker, attorney or your insurer.
- We are not an insurer, agent or broker, and we don't sell insurance.

## Accuracy

We work to keep explanations correct and up to date, but we can't promise that every page is complete, current or right for your situation. Rules and numbers change, and they vary by state. Many explanations are written by AI and checked by a separate AI reviewer; these are marked on the page. If you spot a mistake, please use **Report an issue** on the page.

## Your account

- Keep your sign-in details safe; you are responsible for activity on your account.
- You can delete your account at any time from Account settings.

## Term requests and issue reports

- Requests and reports become public so our writers can work on them. Don't include personal or confidential information.
- Don't send spam, abuse, or anything unlawful. We may remove requests or block accounts that do.

## Our content

The explanations, diagrams and questions on LearnInsurance belong to us or are used with permission. You may read, share links to and quote short parts of them with a link back. Please don't copy whole pages or the glossary in bulk without permission.

## Links to other sites

We link to official sources, such as state insurance departments. We aren't responsible for other sites' content.

## No warranty and limits on liability

The site is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for any loss that comes from relying on the site instead of your policy or professional advice.

## Changes

We may update these terms. If we do, we'll change the date at the top of this page. Using the site after a change means you accept the new terms.

